  date         = {2017-06-07},
  eprintclass  = {cs.SI},
  abstract     = {Low-dimensional embeddings of nodes in large graphs have
                  proved extremely useful in a variety of prediction tasks, from
                  content recommendation to identifying protein functions.
                  However, most existing approaches require that all nodes in
                  the graph are present during training of the embeddings; these
                  previous approaches are inherently transductive and do not
